# The QR signs encode /p/<code>. One document answers every code; the page
# reads the code out of the path.
#
# The destination is deliberately extensionless. Pages serves `found.html` at
# `/found` and 301s `/found.html` to it - and that 301 leaks through a 200
# proxy, which poisons the service worker cache with a redirected response.
# Browsers refuse to serve those for navigations, so a scanned sign died with
# "Response served by service worker has redirections". Naming the canonical
# path here avoids the redirect entirely.
/p/*  /found  200

# /privacy and /qr need no rules: Pages already serves privacy.html and
# qr.html at their extensionless paths.
